            "review_text": "TheodoreDee\n81 contributions\n0\nExtensive menu\nAug 2016 • Couples\nLocated steps from the infamous Thuy Vegetarian restaurant, Hoang Khach stands out being more authentic in terms of ambience, decor AND food options. \n\nWe ordered a few dishes:\n\nCrispy Fried Noodles w/veggies 30,000VND - The \"noodles\" weren't the typical fried egg noodles, it was more like an airy, puff string. Really disappointing.\n\nBun Rieu 20,000VND - delicious broth but not as fresh as I found at Lan Anh.\n\nTempura Fried Tofu 30,000VND - THE BEST dish of the night. Light, crispy batter with a soft tofu core.\n\nSummer Rolls 30,000VND - Fresh tasting with the right amount of veggies but there were zero dipping sauce to accompany the roles.\nRead more\nWritten August 14, 2016",
